# E035: ValueNotSerializable - proxy cannot be serialized to JSON
# NOTE: This error CANNOT be triggered via corpus tests because E035 is only
# raised in value_to_json (lib.rs:207), which is called by the CLI for JSON
# output (main.rs:280), not during evaluation. Corpus tests only test eval_source,
# which does not perform JSON serialization.
#
# This test would need to trigger value_to_json during evaluation, but there is
# no builtin that does this. Possible solutions:
# 1. Add a `to-json` builtin that wraps value_to_json
# 2. Extend corpus test infrastructure to support post-eval JSON serialization
# 3. Accept that E035 can only be tested via unit tests in lib.rs (currently done)
#
# COVERAGE STATUS: E035 is tested via unit tests in src/lib.rs:
# - test_json_proxy_error (line 552): validates E035 message and code

# This placeholder test demonstrates proxy behavior but does NOT test E035.
# It tests E080 (UserError from $raise builtin) instead.
[p: [proxy [fn [let key] [raise "handler called"]]]  result: p.test]
